From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] journal: defer reattach while toolbar is still rooted

Journal Detail and Main views swap their toolbars during Escape navigation.
GTK4 may leave a detached toolbar rooted until the dispatch cycle completes;
appending it immediately then aborts in gtk_widget_root().  Defer only that
transient reattach, matching the canvas protection.

--- a/src/jarabe/journal/journalwindow.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/journal/journalwindow.py
@@ -89,5 +89,8 @@
             if toolbar.get_parent() == self._toolbar_area:
                 return
             if toolbar.get_parent() != self._toolbar_area:
                 parent = toolbar.get_parent()
                 if parent != self._toolbar_area:
                     parent.remove(toolbar)
             if toolbar.get_parent() != self._toolbar_area:
+                if toolbar.get_root() is not None:
+                    GLib.idle_add(self.set_toolbar_box, toolbar)
+                    return
                 self._toolbar_area.append(toolbar)
